[1106.8s]   💬 **Key technical decisions during the build:**
[1106.8s]   💬 - The recurring trap was **volumetric wash** — a deep/emissive nebula viewed along its depth integrates to flat pale-green fog. Solved with a *thin backdrop slab* lit mostly by the tower (emission 0), so far corners stay near-black while the tower plume lights nearby wisps.
[1106.8s]   💬 - Recomposed the camera from a downward "aerial" tilt to near-level so the **horizon drops to the lower third** (sky-dominant), matching the reference far better.
[1106.8s]   💬 - A dedicated **crown-fountain volume** gives the billowing green plume and masks the sign block.
[1106.8s]   💬 The deterministic rebuild lives at `build/M1.py` — imports + normalizes the frozen hero mesh, rebuilds all materials/volumes/lights/camera/grade, and re-runs cleanly from an empty scene (2.2s, ~258k tris, no per-element loops — all repeated elements are single instanced objects).
